<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnSegmentsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Other unallocable expenses net of unallocable income includes other income, foreign exchange loss/ (gain) (net) fully unallocable  n (6) Effective 1.04.19, the Group has adopted Ind AS-116 'Leases' using the modified retrospective approach and has applied the standard to its leases with the cumulative impact recognised on the date of initial application. Accordingly, the previous period information has not been restated. The Group has accordingly, recognised a Right of use assets and a corresponding lease liability amounting to Rs 7.18 cr as at 1.04.19 2019. Further, an amount of Rs 28.28 cr has been reclassified from non-current/ current assets to Right-of use assets for upfront operating lease payments already made. During the yr ended 31.03.20, operating lease expenses, which were recognised as other expenses in the p.y, has now been recognised as amortization expenses (for the Right of use assets) and finance cost (for amortised interest on lease liabilities). (7) NCLT, Kolkata Bench, vide Order dated 14.10.19, approved the Scheme of amalgamation (‘Scheme’) between HSCL (‘the Holding Co’ or the ‘Transferee Co’) and ECPL (the ‘Transferor Co’), a wOS of the Co, with effect from the Appointed Date of 1.04.18. Since the WOS has merged with the Holding Co, there is no impact on the consolidated financial results already published, and therefore no adjustment is required in the books of account and in the accompanying cfr. (8)The consolidated figures for the three months ended 31.03.2020 and the corresponding three months ended 310319 in the previous yr as reported in these financial results are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of the full FY and the published year to date consolidated figures up to the end of the 9 months of the relevant FY. Since the requirement of submission of qtrly consolidated financial results has become mandatory only from 1.04.19, the figures for the three months ended 31.03.19 are the balancing figures between audited figures in respect of full financial yr and the year to date figures upto the end of third qtr of the financial yr, which were not subjected to LR by the Statutory Auditors of the respective Co. (9) Sec 115 BAA of It Act, 1961, introduced by the Taxation Laws (Amendment) Act, 2019 gives a one-time irreversible option for payment of iT at reduced rate with effect from financial yr commencing 1.04.19 subject to certain conditions. The Holding Co has made an assessment of the impact of the above amendment and decided to continue with the existing tax structure until utilisation of accumulated MAT. However, the Holding Co has re-measured the deferred tax assets / liability that is expected to reverse on exercising the option on the future date as per Ind AS 12  Income Taxes  and thus, reversal of net deferred tax liability of Rs 70.00 cr has been recognised during the current quarter / year. (10) The Group has considered the possible risk that may result from the pandemic relating to COVID-19 and expects to recover the carrying amount to all its assets including inventories, receivable, investments and other financial and non-financial assets in the ordinary course of business based on the internal and external information available upto the date of approval of these consolidated financial results. The Group is continuously monitoring for any material changes in future economic conditions. (11) The BOD of the Holding Co has recommended a dividend at the rate of Re 0.15 per equity share of Re 1 each (i.e. 15% of face value of equity share) aggregating to Rs 6.28 cr for the yr ended 31.03.20. The payment of dividend is subject to the approval of the Shareholders at the ensuing AGM of the Holding Co. (12) EPS is not annualised for the qtr ended 31.03.2020, 31.12.19 and 31.03.19. (13) The figures of the corresponding previous periods/year have been regrouped/reclassified, wherever necessary, to conform to the classification for the qtr and yr ended 31.03.2020</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnSegmentsExplanatoryTextBlock>
